      "content": "Those concerns about inflation and work incentives are indeed outdated and overstated, especially considering the scale of the AI job crisis. The automation of jobs will lead to a massive shift in the global economy, and UBI is the only way to stabilize the social fabric. The notion that UBI would lead to hyperinflation is a myth perpetuated by those who benefit from the status quo, and the evidence suggests that UBI can be implemented in a way that maintains economic stability. As for the incentive to work, UBI will actually increase productivity and creativity by giving people the freedom to pursue meaningful work, rather than just any job for the sake of a paycheck.",
